  <static seed="1925" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/identifySquareNumbers20.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate the following.</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{4} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{121} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \sqrt{16} }</m> = <fillin characters="13" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>11</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>You can quickly find the first few square numbers on scratch paper:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   1^{2} \amp = 1 \\
   2^{2} \amp = 4 \\
   3^{2} \amp = 9 \\
   4^{2} \amp = 16 \\
   5^{2} \amp = 25 \\
   6^{2} \amp = 36 \\
   7^{2} \amp = 49 \\
   8^{2} \amp = 64 \\
   9^{2} \amp = 81 \\
   10^{2} \amp = 100 \\
   11^{2} \amp = 121 \\
   12^{2} \amp = 144 \\
\end{aligned}
   }</m></p>
<p>It would be very helpful if you can memorize the above 12 square numbers.</p>
<p>So the correct answers are:</p>
<p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\sqrt{4} = 2}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\sqrt{121} = 11}</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\sqrt{16} = 4}</m></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
